Z||000002||Old Lar||08-24-2000||11:59 AM||||Ed Parks (the Fiero Factory)in Toney Alabama is one of your closest good Fiero mechanics who has done swaps.  Costs vary, but expect to pay several grand for the job, more if you need a good engine.<P>Its not a just switch engine job. Need wiring, ecm, transmission flex plate or clutch assembly and maybe axles, exhaust.  You should upgrade brakes and suspension to handle the new HP.<P>Check the archives on 3800 swaps.. Lots of information.<P>And if you are going to spend the $$ to do it right, you don't want a 100000 mile replacement engine.  Expect to pay more than you want to.||||reg||1
